{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Three times you shall keep a festival to Me in the year.</b> And He turned back again and mentioned here: ״three times in the year all your males shall appear,״ and it is said in another place (Exodus 23:17): ״שלש פעמים בשנה יראה כל זכורך״ וגו׳ ״בחג המצות ובחג השבועות ובחג הסכות״ — here He said רגלים without specification and did not spell out ״בחג המצות ובחג השבועות״ וכו׳; I would say that one should go there three times in the year within three or four months — and therefore it says ״בחג המצות ובחג השבועות ובחג הסוכות״; if so, why is it said רגלים in the language of רגלים? This excludes those who ride on beasts — to exclude the lame and the blind and the sick and the old and the young, who cannot go up on their feet." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> ״שלש פעמים״ — ״שלש רגלים״, and elsewhere it says (Isaiah 26:6): ״תרמסנה רגל רגלי עני פעמי דלים״ — a warning to Israel that they should not go up except on their feet. And thus Scripture says (Song of Songs 7:2): ״מה יפו פעמיך בנעלים בת נדיב״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:19.969673331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}